  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe donor's tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) is six percent (6%) on the total gifts exceeding Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Pesos (₱250,000).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is governed by Section 99 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that the tax for each calendar year shall be six percent (6%) computed on the basis of the total gifts in excess of ₱250,000.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder the TRAIN law, any gifts made by an individual that exceed the exemption threshold of ₱250,000 are subject to a donor's tax rate of 6%. This means that if the total value of gifts given in a calendar year is less than or equal to ₱250,000, no donor's tax is due. However, any amount above this threshold will be taxed at the specified rate.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, individuals making gifts should keep track of the total value of their gifts throughout the year. If the cumulative value exceeds ₱250,000, they will need to file a donor's tax return and pay the corresponding tax on the excess amount. This provision encourages individuals to be mindful of their gifting activities, especially in terms of tax implications.",
